---
import config from '../../site-config.json';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import StatsBar from '../components/StatsBar.astro';
import WhyChooseUs from '../components/WhyChooseUs.astro';
import Testimonials from '../components/Testimonials.astro';
import FAQ from '../components/FAQ.astro';
import FinalCTA from '../components/FinalCTA.astro';

const { meta, colors, typography, header, footer, stats, whyChooseUs, testimonials, faq, finalCta } = config;

const pageTitle = 'About Us | ILM Assignment Help';
const pageDescription = "Learn who's behind ILM Assignment Help: a specialist team supporting City & Guilds ILM candidates from Level 2 to Level 7 with work-based evidence, reflective accounts, and criterion-referenced writing.";

const aboutFaq = faq.items.slice(0, 4);
---

<Layout
  title={pageTitle}
  description={pageDescription}
  faviconPath={meta.faviconPath}
  googleFontsUrl={meta.googleFontsUrl}
  fontFamily={typography.fontFamily}
  colors={colors}
>
  <Header logoText={header.logoText} logoHref="/" navLinks={header.navLinks} />

  <PageHero
    badge="Company"
    crumbLabel="About Us"
    h1="About ILM Assignment Help"
    intro="We are a specialist assignment support service built around one qualification family: City & Guilds ILM leadership and management qualifications, from Level 2 through to Level 7 and the Coaching & Mentoring pathway."
    ctaLabel={header.ctaButton.label}
    ctaHref={header.ctaButton.href}
  />

  <StatsBar stats={stats} />

  <main class="page-content">
    <div class="container page-content--narrow-inner">
      <article class="prose">
        <h2>Who We Are</h2>
        <p>
          ILM Assignment Help is a specialist writing and academic support service for candidates studying City & Guilds
          ILM leadership and management qualifications. We do not offer generic essay-writing help across every subject.
          We work exclusively within the ILM qualification framework, which means every writer on our team understands
          how ILM units are structured, how assessment criteria are worded, and what the difference is between a
          submission that passes and one that reaches Distinction.
        </p>
        <p>
          That focus matters because ILM assessment is not a conventional academic essay format. It is criterion-referenced
          and work-based: assignments are marked against specific, numbered assessment criteria, and every criterion has
          to be evidenced individually from the candidate's own workplace practice. Missing one criterion results in a
          referral regardless of how strong the rest of the submission is. Generic academic writers who have not worked
          inside this assessment model consistently miss that distinction, which is the single most common reason ILM
          submissions come back referred.
        </p>

        <h2>Our Writers and Their ILM Background</h2>
        <p>
          Every writer we work with has direct, practical familiarity with ILM units, learning outcomes, and grade
          descriptors across Levels 2 to 7. That includes the work-based evidence standards ILM assessors apply, the
          reflective practice frameworks ILM units expect (Gibbs, Kolb, and Schön), and the Harvard referencing
          conventions required from Level 4 upward. Writers are matched to orders based on the specific ILM level and
          unit involved, not assigned generically.
        </p>
        <p>
          We do not use writers whose only experience is general management essay writing. ILM's assessment model
          rewards candidates who can connect theory to real, evidenced workplace practice, and that is the specific
          skill our writers are selected for.
        </p>

        <h2>Coverage Across Every ILM Level and Pathway</h2>
        <p>
          Support is available across the full ILM qualification ladder: Level 2 introductory awards, Level 3 team
          leader and first-line supervisor units, Level 4 junior middle management units, Level 5 middle management and
          operations units, Level 6 professional management units, and Level 7 senior leadership and strategic units.
          The Coaching and Mentoring pathway is supported separately at Levels 3, 5, and 7, including coaching session
          logs, coaching philosophy statements, and supervision documentation.
        </p>

        <h2>What "ILM-Standard" Actually Means</h2>
      </article>

      <div class="info-grid">
        <div class="info-card">
          <h3 class="info-card__title"><span class="info-card__icon">📋</span> Criterion-by-criterion coverage</h3>
          <p class="info-card__desc">Every assessment criterion in the unit specification is identified and explicitly addressed, not inferred by the assessor from general coverage of the topic.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="info-card">
          <h3 class="info-card__title"><span class="info-card__icon">🗂️</span> Genuine work-based evidence structure</h3>
          <p class="info-card__desc">Written analysis is structured to connect to real workplace evidence, with clear annotation showing how each piece of evidence maps to a specific criterion.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="info-card">
          <h3 class="info-card__title"><span class="info-card__icon">📚</span> Harvard referencing as standard</h3>
          <p class="info-card__desc">Correctly formatted in-text citations and reference lists from Level 4 upward, with peer-reviewed journal sourcing where Level 7 requires it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="info-card">
          <h3 class="info-card__title"><span class="info-card__icon">🔍</span> Turnitin originality report</h3>
          <p class="info-card__desc">Every completed assignment is checked before delivery, and a copy of the originality report is provided alongside the finished work.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <article class="prose">
        <h2>Confidentiality and Academic Integrity</h2>
        <p>
          Orders are kept confidential. Your identity, employer, and workplace details are never shared outside the
          writer and reviewer assigned to your order, and nothing you submit to us is resold or reused for anyone else.
          We are explicit about where our support sits relative to academic integrity: our guidance is structured to
          develop your understanding of what your ILM criteria require and how to evidence your own management
          practice, in the same way a model answer, study coach, or tutor would. The management experience being
          evidenced in your submission is your own; our role is the structured writing and analytical support that
          helps you present it to the standard your assessor expects. For the full detail on this boundary, see our
          <a href="/ilm-academic-integrity-policy/">ILM academic integrity policy</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Revisions Until Your Criteria Are Met</h2>
        <p>
          If an assignment comes back needing changes, revisions are unlimited and free within 14 days of delivery.
          Full detail on how revisions and refunds work is set out in our
          <a href="/our-policy/">service policy</a> and <a href="/refund-policy/">refund policy</a>.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>

  <WhyChooseUs heading={whyChooseUs.heading} items={whyChooseUs.items} />
  <Testimonials heading={testimonials.heading} items={testimonials.items} />
  <FAQ sectionId="about-faq" heading="Common Questions About Us" items={aboutFaq} />

  <FinalCTA heading={finalCta.heading} subtext={finalCta.subtext} button={finalCta.button} />
  <Footer
    logoText={footer.logoText}
    description={footer.description}
    columns={footer.columns}
    copyright={footer.copyright}
    contactEmail={footer.contactEmail}
    whatsapp={footer.whatsapp}
  />
</Layout>

<style>
  .page-content--narrow-inner {
    max-width: 820px;
  }
</style>
